ot cite the paced transit as browser-confirmed. Opening-only scope — enclosure/M249 page separation awaits owner clarification.\n  - **Historical paper breakthrough revision 2026-10-01 — technical packet recorded 2026-10-02; superseded by the owner's causal portal correction.** The brief supersedes the vellum / electrical-outline / late-fade opening with a real opaque paper barrier: hairline exact-profile slit .66–.79 (`crackGlow`, lit through pressure and fracture), `pressure` smooth01 .79–.84, `fracture` smooth01 .84–.88, `crackWeb` = pressure·(1−fracture), `openingClear` only from .88, fragments clear by .88; `illumination` .88–.89 arrives before `pbr` .89–.91 (metal .89, fully PBR .91); model rise from .89; lamp return .79–.86, perspective .90 and `INTRO_SCROLL_SHARE` .50 retained. `drawingOpacity` is permanently 1 (no fade; `paperVellum()` returns 0) and the perforated sheet remains through global .18 and exits physically .18–.22. `relativePose` now translates by `u^1.4` and preserves the registered side rotation throughout the lift; the camera supplies orbit. The solved clearance is .692509 pose (intro .919791917); legacy wave fields remain trigger-only and disabled. Static gates for this revision: 184/184 tests (the opening/paper contract tests were revised with the behavior). Full six-case browser roster and review media checks PASS; fresh technical review SHIP, and everything under the storm folders is historical. Owner visual acceptance and close-out remain open; no commit or push.\n  - **Active portal correction 2026-10-02 — TECHNICALLY VERIFIED 2026-10-02; owner review OPEN.** [Plan](docs/jgun-portal-correction-plan.md). J-Gun pressure push .79–.84 causes the bulge; illumination .79–.81 and PBR .80–.82 resolve before first fracture .84. Rupture .84–.88 immediately exposes the J-Gun, with continuous rise .79–1. Opaque portal depth and irregular descending walls replace wood in every visible profile gap; white-blue light catches torn undersides and metal, 